Fetch a URL. HTML comes back as readable markdown (boilerplate stripped) by default; `format` can ask for `text` or raw `html`, and JSON is indented. Pages over {{ .MaxFetchSizeKB }}KB are saved to a file for view/grep rather than truncated. Pass `download: true` to stream the response to a file instead of reading it into context - that is the way to get an archive, image or PDF, and it is binary-safe. Saved files land in this session's scratch directory, never in the working tree. No AI processing: for a question spread over several pages use research.
{{- if .GhAvailable }} For GitHub content when an exact repo, issue, or PR link is provided, use `gh` CLI in bash instead.{{- end }}
